#### Variation 3: GraphQL Federation

**Use Case**: Clients need flexible querying, backend services expose GraphQL schemas

**Implementation**: Apollo Federation gateway

```graphql
# Gateway schema
type Provider {
  id: ID!
  name: String!
  npi: String!
  credentialing: CredentialingStatus @resolve(from: "credentialing-service")
  claimsStats: ClaimsStatistics @resolve(from: "claims-service")
  payments: PaymentSummary @resolve(from: "payments-service")
}

type Query {
  providerDashboard(providerId: ID!): Provider
}
```

**Client Query:**
```graphql
query GetProviderDashboard($providerId: ID!) {
  providerDashboard(providerId: $providerId) {
    id
    name
    credentialing {
      status
      expirationDate
    }
    claimsStats(period: THIRTY_DAYS) {
      totalClaims
      paidAmount
    }
  }
}
```

**Pros**: Flexible client queries, strong typing, industry standard
**Cons**: Requires GraphQL adoption, learning curve, query complexity management

